export const northstarBrief = `NORTHSTAR CONSULTING
Website brief - first release

Business
Northstar Consulting helps small service businesses improve their operations, simplify internal processes and plan sustainable growth. The website should encourage prospective clients to enquire about working together.

Pages
1. Home: headline, short introduction, three service summaries and a prominent contact button.
2. Services: describe business strategy, process improvement and ongoing advisory support. Each service should lead visitors to the Contact page.
3. Contact: a short introductory paragraph and a form with name, email and message fields. Successful enquiries should arrive in the business inbox. The visitor should see a clear confirmation after submitting.

Design
A clean, professional and welcoming appearance. Use the supplied logo and navy, teal and off-white colours. Avoid clutter. Text and buttons should be easy to read and use on mobile.

Content
The client will supply the final logo, page text and images before the two-week delivery period begins. The professional will place and format the supplied content. Original copywriting and photography are not included.

Budget and timing
Fixed project budget: USD 600.
Target delivery: within two weeks of milestone approval and receipt of the required content and access.
One consolidated round of minor design and text-placement revisions is included.

First-release boundaries
Three public pages only. No customer accounts, online appointment booking, payment collection, blog or ecommerce in this release.

Completion expectations
All three pages work on desktop and mobile. Navigation and contact buttons work. Required form fields are validated. A test enquiry reaches the confirmed recipient inbox. A success message is displayed after successful submission.`;
